; XSpark - XAUUSD M5 "survival" profile
; Derived from the 2026.01.01-2026.09.18 real-tick backtest (1162 positions).
;
; WHY THE REFERENCE RUN COLLAPSED
; That run was +73R gross yet lost 91% of the account. Cause was sizing, not
; signals: 3% risk per trade with up to 5 SIMULTANEOUS positions that were in
; the same direction 100% of the time - one bet of up to 15% of equity - while
; InpUseTotalDDKillSwitch was set to false. Measured edge is +0.063R per trade
; (t = 1.17), which is not significant and cannot carry that sizing.
; Growth-optimal (full Kelly) risk on this R distribution is ~2.0% for ONE
; position; the run was effectively 7x past that.
;
; WHAT THIS PROFILE CHANGES: position sizing and the safety rails ONLY.
; Entry logic and stop/target geometry are left exactly as tested, so the
; measured R distribution still applies.
; Replay on the same trade sequence: 5,000 -> 5,183, max DD 22.6% (was 99.8%).
; This is deliberately near-breakeven. It is a survival profile: it proves the
; account lives through the full period. See xauusd-m5-thursday-off.set for the
; version that actually makes money, and the notes on what still needs testing.

InpEnableTrading=true
InpEntryStyle=0
InpAutoTuneForSymbol=true
InpMinScore=3.0

; --- the core fix: one small bet, not five stacked correlated ones ---
InpMaxOpenTrades=2
InpRiskPctTier1=0.35
InpRiskPctTier2=0.35
InpRiskPctTier3=0.35
InpMaxRiskPct=0.5
InpMaxAccountRiskPct=1.0

; --- restore the rails the EA ships with ---
InpMaxDailyDDPct=6.0
InpUseTotalDDKillSwitch=true
InpMaxTotalDDPct=25.0

; --- UNCHANGED from the reference run (do not tune these in the same test) ---
InpATRMultSL=3.0
InpMinRR=3.0
InpMaxRR=10.0
InpPartialTPRatio=2.5
InpPartialClosePct=50.0
InpATRMultTrail=1.0
InpUsePinBars=true
InpPatternMaxChaseATR=1
